   "title": "Jung Ho-yeon named among potential Bond girls, raising prospect of Korean first",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/lifestyle/people-events/20261117/jung-ho-yeon-named-among-potential-bond-girls-raising-prospect-of-korean-first",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:57:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794905822.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Korean actress Jung Ho-yeon, who rose to global fame through Netflix's \"Squid Game,\" has been named among 45 actresses suggested by U.S. fashion magazine Vogue as potential Bond girls for the next James Bond film, raising the possibility that she could become the first Korean actress to take on the role. Jung was named alongside prominent Hollywood actresses including Margaret Qualley, Zendaya and Florence Pugh, placing her among a diverse group of potential candidates suggested by the magazine.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国演员郑浩妍通过 Netflix 的《鱿鱼游戏》走向全球 fame 后，被美国时尚杂志 Vogue 列为下一部詹姆斯·邦德电影潜在“邦德女郎”的45名女演员之一，这意味着她有可能成为首位饰演这一角色的韩国女演员。郑浩妍与玛格丽特·奎利、赞达亚和弗洛伦丝·皮尤等知名好莱坞女演员一同获提名，跻身该杂志提出的多元化候选人行列。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korean actress Jung Ho-yeon, who rose to global fame through Netflix's \"Squid Game,\" has been named among 45 actresses suggested by U.S. fashion magazine Vogue as potential Bond girls for the next James Bond film, raising the possibility that she could become the first Korean actress to take on the role. The speculation comes as Hollywood actor Robert Pattinson has been named the next James Bond, drawing attention to who might star opposite him in the upcoming installment of the long-running spy franchise. On Sunday, Vogue published a list of 45 actresses it considered suitable for the next Bond film, placing Jung fifth on the list. The magazine highlighted Jung's breakout performance in \"Squid Game\" and her appearance in director Na Hong-jin's film \"Hope.\" It suggested that Jung could be a strong choice for a Bond girl if the next 007 film expands its setting to Asia. However, the list represents Vogue's own predictions and does not indicate that Amazon MGM Studios, which oversees the franchise, is officially considering Jung for the role. Jung gained international recognition in 2021 for playing Kang Sae-byeok, a North Korean defector, in the first season of Netflix's global hit \"Squid Game.\" The series' worldwide success brought her recognition at international awards ceremonies and helped launch her Hollywood career. The film follows mysterious events that unfold after a tiger is reportedly spotted in a village near the Demilitarized Zone separating the two Koreas. It attracted international attention after being invited to compete at the 79th Cannes Film Festival. Jung was named alongside prominent Hollywood actresses including Margaret Qualley, Zendaya and Florence Pugh, placing her among a diverse group of potential candidates suggested by the magazine. Although Asian actresses have previously appeared as Bond girls, no Korean actress has held the role. Malaysian actress Michelle Yeoh starred opposite Pierce Brosnan in the 1997 film \"Tomorrow Never Dies.\" If Jung were cast in the next installment, she would become the first Korean actress to play a Bond girl in the franchise's history. Meanwhile, Amazon MGM Studios announced on Monday (local time) that Pattinson would play James Bond in the franchise's 26th film. Best known for his roles in the \"Twilight\" franchise and \"The Batman,\" Pattinson would become the seventh actor to portray Bond in the official theatrical film series. This article from the Hankook Ilbo, the sister publication of The Korea Times, was translated by a generative AI system and edited by The Korea Times",
