   "title": "Bandits Kill 37-Year-Old Chinese Miner, Police Inspector In Bauchi",
   "url": "https://www.channelstv.com/2026/11/16/bandits-kill-37-year-old-chinese-miner-police-inspector-in-bauchi",
   "domain": "channelstv.com",
   "source": "channelstv.com",
   "published": "Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:39:19 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794861559.0,
   "ageDays": 0.53,
   "summary": "Suspected bandits have killed a 37-year-old Chinese national, Wang Tingjian, who worked with Zurfi Mining Company, and his police escort, Inspector Abba Ya’u, attached to MOPOL 34, Gombe State, in an ambush in Bauchi State. Confirming the incident to Channels Television in a telephone interview on Monday, the Police Public Relations Officer (PPRO), SP Nafiu Habib, said the Chinese miner was conducting a survey at a mining site when he and his escort were attacked by suspected gunmen.",
   "summary_zh": "涉嫌武装劫匪在包奇州伏击并杀害了一名在 Zurfi Mining Company 工作的37岁中国籍男子王廷健，以及其警察护送人员、隶属贡贝州 MOPOL 34 的阿巴·亚乌督察。周一，警方公共关系官（PPRO）纳菲乌·哈比卜警司在电话采访中向 Channels Television 证实了此事。他说，这名中国矿工当时正在一处采矿点开展勘测工作，他和护送人员随后遭涉嫌持枪歹徒袭击。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Suspected bandits have killed a 37-year-old Chinese national, Wang Tingjian, who worked with Zurfi Mining Company, and his police escort, Inspector Abba Ya’u, attached to MOPOL 34, Gombe State, in an ambush in Bauchi State. The incident occurred on Saturday at about 1:30 p.m. in Ruga Village, Gwana District, Alkaleri Local Government Area of the state. Confirming the incident to Channels Television in a telephone interview on Monday, the Police Public Relations Officer (PPRO), SP Nafiu Habib, said the Chinese miner was conducting a survey at a mining site when he and his escort were attacked by suspected gunmen. He explained that the attack triggered an exchange of gunfire between the security operatives and the assailants. “During the survey, they were ambushed by unknown gunmen. The Chinese national had even run towards the vehicle conveying them for safety, but they were overwhelmed,” Habib said. According to the PPRO, the victims were rushed to the Federal Teaching Hospital, Gombe, where they were confirmed dead and their bodies deposited in the hospital’s mortuary. Habib further disclosed that the anti-kidnapping unit and the Violent Crime Response Unit, in collaboration with the military and local vigilantes, were conducting a manhunt for the attackers. He added that security agencies were also working to unravel the circumstances surrounding the incident. STAY INFORMED NAIJA CONNECT Every week, discover the stories of progress at home and excellence around the world",
