   "published": "Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:34:06 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794884646.0,
   "ageDays": 0.26,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The government late Monday (November 16, 2026) hiked the export duty on diesel and aviation turbine fuel (ATF) by ₹2.5 per litre and ₹1.5 per litre, whilst keeping the levy on export of petrol unchanged at nil. Duty rates on petrol and diesel meant for domestic consumption remain unchanged. In the upcoming fortnight, diesel exports would draw a levy of ₹14 per litre compared to ₹11.5 per litre mandated for the previous fortnight.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁这些内容。政府于2026年11月16日星期一晚将柴油和航空涡轮燃料（ATF）的出口关税分别上调至每升2.5卢比和每升1.5卢比，同时继续将汽油出口税维持在零。供国内消费的汽油和柴油税率保持不变。在即将到来的两周内，柴油出口将适用每升14卢比的税负，而此前两周规定的税额为每升11.5卢比。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The government late Monday (November 16, 2026) hiked the export duty on diesel and aviation turbine fuel (ATF) by ₹2.5 per litre and ₹1.5 per litre, whilst keeping the levy on export of petrol unchanged at nil. Duty rates on petrol and diesel meant for domestic consumption remain unchanged. The hike in diesel levy assumes added significance as India looks to further up their exports of the vehicular fuel to Europe amid a global supply crunch. In the upcoming fortnight, diesel exports would draw a levy of ₹14 per litre compared to ₹11.5 per litre mandated for the previous fortnight. ATF exports would draw a levy of ₹12.5 per litre against ₹11 per litre. The government has been conducting a fortnightly review of export levies since March 27, in the backdrop of the conflict in West Asia. These are done based on the average international benchmark prices of crude oil, petrol, diesel and ATF observed since the previous review. This is to ensure the domestic availability of retail fuels by disincentivising exports. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
