   "title": "2027: Kaduna Govt Gives APC Chairmen Vehicles For Campaign",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/2027-kaduna-govt-gives-apc-chairmen-vehicles-for-campaign/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:17:12 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794824232.0,
   "ageDays": 0.96,
   "summary": "Sadiq Mamman Lagos, who presented the vehicles on behalf of the state government, charged the beneficiaries to use them for grassroots mobilisation and ensure electoral victory for the party. He urged the beneficiaries to use the vehicles for peaceful, issue-based campaigns, voter education and public enlightenment.",
   "summary_zh": "萨迪克·马曼在拉各斯代表州政府交付这些车辆，并要求受益者利用车辆开展基层动员，确保该党赢得选举。他敦促受益者使用车辆开展和平、以议题为导向的宣传，以及选民教育和公众启蒙。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The commissioner for local government and chieftaincy affairs, Hon. Sadiq Mamman Lagos, who presented the vehicles on behalf of the state government, charged the beneficiaries to use them for grassroots mobilisation and ensure electoral victory for the party. He said the distribution was part of efforts to strengthen the party’s structures and enable its officials to reach communities, wards and polling units to canvass support for APC candidates. Mamman Lagos said similar distributions had been carried out in Zones Two and Three, adding that the exercise aimed to improve the party’s mobilisation capacity across the state. “We have done Zones Two and Three, and now we are doing Zone One. We are distributing these vehicles to you because we want you to deliver Zone One to us,” he said. He urged the beneficiaries to use the vehicles for peaceful, issue-based campaigns, voter education and public enlightenment. The commissioner also charged them with visiting communities, explaining the programmes and achievements of APC-led governments, and convincing residents to support the party through constructive engagement. Also speaking, former Kaduna State Governor and APC senatorial candidate for Kaduna North, Mukhtar Ramalan Yero, described the distribution as a welcome development, saying logistical support was necessary for effective grassroots mobilisation. He said the vehicles would enable party officials to reach communities and canvass support for candidates ahead of the elections. Yero urged party members to remain loyal to the leadership and work together to strengthen the party’s structures ahead of the 2027 elections. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
